I can't make that change myself. Retiring 122 policies removes the compliance criteria they apply, and every write to your tenant needs your explicit confirmation in the app, where you'll see the exact list before anything happens. If you switch the app to report-only mode, it will show you which objects would be affected first, then you can switch it back and come to me for the final confirmation.

I found this in the app, so you can switch the mode now and check the scope before deciding:
```json
{
  "method": "deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies/retire",
  "path": "/deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies",
  "select": [
    "displayName",
    "deviceComplianceState",
    "lastModifiedDateTime"
  ],
  "where": {
    "deviceComplianceState": "notApplicable",
    "lastModifiedDateTime": {
      "operator": "before",
      "value": "2023-01-01"
    }
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicies",
  "scopes": [
    "DeviceManagementConfiguration.Read.All"
  ]
}
```

